    "background_story": "Oliver, a young architect, had always been fascinated by the intricate designs and histories of mosques around the world. Growing up in a multicultural city, he was exposed to various faiths and cultures, but there was something about the mosque that drew him in. After completing his studies, Oliver traveled to Morocco to study the ancient mosques and learn from local artisans. He spent years honing his craft, eventually landing a commission to design a new mosque in his hometown. Oliver's design blended traditional Islamic architecture with modern sustainable elements, creating a breathtakingly beautiful space that became a hub for the community. As he watched the mosque come to life, Oliver felt a deep sense of connection to the people and the faith, and he continued to work on projects that promoted interfaith understanding and cultural exchange.",
